# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Line endings.
#
# Added 2026-11-22, when SearXNG's installer had to run on a Windows VPS. A
# shell script checked out with CRLF on Windows fails the moment it reaches
# Linux (WSL, a container, a real VPS) with `$'\r': command not found`, which
# names neither the file nor the cause. Pinning .sh to LF means the file is the
# same bytes everywhere, whatever a clone's core.autocrlf says.
#
# .ps1 is deliberately NOT pinned: PowerShell is happy with either, and the
# scripts under infra/ are written as ASCII with a BOM, which is what makes
# Windows PowerShell 5.1 read them as UTF-8 rather than the ANSI codepage.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

*.sh text eol=lf
